-- examples/checks/sealed-provenance.rofl — THE ONE KNOB. A world that declares
-- sealed(provenance) asks for the set of facts and nothing about how they were
-- reached: no derived_by, and in the Rust engine no witness either, so a step
-- is a new fact rather than a firing (f_the_set_of_facts_is_the_contract_and_any_support_will_do_for_facts_about_code).
-- The engine's own order of groups, candidates and activation and its walk of
-- a closure are defaults wherever nothing withdraws, seal or no seal. Both
-- engines must conclude the same rows: reach is a closure with a cycle (c, d)
-- and a diamond (a to d by two paths).
sealed(provenance).
edb(edge).
edge(a, b). edge(b, d). edge(a, c). edge(c, d). edge(d, c). edge(d, e).
reach(X, Y) :- edge(X, Y).
reach(X, Z) :- reach(X, Y), edge(Y, Z).
loops(X) :- reach(X, X).
far(X, Y) :- reach(X, Y), not edge(X, Y).
